# Forms & mail

- Validate on **client and server**. Never trust HTML `required` alone.
- Reject spam patterns: random Latin strings, disposable-looking bulk mail, invalid RU phones, empty/garbage messages.
- RU phone: normalize to digits; expect `7` + 10 digits (or clear international rules). Mask UI ≠ validation.
- Server (`sendMail`): schema (e.g. zod), honeypot field, rate limit, optional Turnstile later.
- SMTP credentials only from `runtimeConfig` / env. Never commit passwords.
- Outbound mail: branded HTML template + plain-text fallback; include name, phone, email, message, timestamp.
- Do not log full PII unnecessarily; never echo secrets in error responses.
